def feature(item, bins, capacity):
    """Normalised position of each candidate in the oldest-first lineup: pos/(k-1), 0 for the oldest, 1 for the new bin."""
    k = bins.shape[0]
    if k <= 1:
        return np.zeros(k, dtype=float)
    return np.arange(k, dtype=float) / (k - 1)
```

This computes a pure position ramp: each candidate's index in the oldest-first lineup divided by `k-1`, so the oldest bin scores 0.0 and the brand-new empty bin (always last) scores 1.0, with 0.0 returned for all candidates when there is only one. It depends only on position, not on item size or residual, exactly as specified.

